  "body": "I think it would be nice to make the ```<cite>``` element more \"meaningful\". From what I understand, it doesn't \"do\" much besides helping CSS abbreviations and maybe a few web scrappers.\r\n\r\nI think adding a ```urn``` (Uniform Resource Name) could be useful for citation plugins and academic tools.\r\n\r\nIn the example below, such a plugin could auto generate the link for the cited work, generate a list of cited works or provide a tooltip with useful information.\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<p>According to a study called <cite urn=\"doi:10.1001/archinternmed.2009.384\">\r\nMental Morbidities and Chronic Fatigue in Severe\r\nAcute Respiratory Syndrome Survivors</cite>, people\r\nwho got SARS may develop long term diseases.<p>\r\n```",
